ould ask george he will say  he stopped writing on the show because  he wanted to focus on finishing the wins  of winner  but i don't think that's entirely  accurate after he stopped writing  episodes in season 4  george went on to help create other  shows and write other books  so if he was too busy writing the wins  of winner to write for game of thrones  then how did he have all this time to do  these other things as well as attending  many different conventions over the  years  this is only speculation but i think his  relationship  with dan and dave started to  disintegrate as they went further and  further away from his books  when you think about it this was right  around the same time he stopped writing  for the show  season 5 was the first season he did not  write an episode  and that was when the show really  started to separate itself from the  books  i think he did not want to associate  himself with that version of the story  but like i said  this is only a guess obviously i don't  know what really happened behind the  scenes  regardless of what happened i still love  the show for many years after that  and i still love the books either way i  have still wondered how george felt  about the show  after he left he is still creating shows  for hbo  like house of the dragon so i'm afraid  we won't find out anytime  soon as long as george is under contract  by hbo  i don't think he will reveal how he  really feels but george has now gone on  record and said what his  least favorite scene is let me show you  what he said then i will give you my  thoughts because i do think there is a  reason why he chose this scene  instead of so many others that had a  greater impact on the story  the article from entertainment weekly  says george rr martin has a least  favorite scene in game of thrones  and it's probably not the one you'd  expect in my new book fire cannot kill a  dragon  the song of ice and fire saga author  candidly discusses many aspects of hbo's  hit series  he has high praise for many elements of  the epic adaptation  such as the show's staging annette  stark's death and the red  wedding but occasionally he's critical  as well  martin reveals his least favorite scene  came in the show's first season  when the production struggled with a  budget that was very large for 2011  roughly 6 million each episode but still  not large enough to stage many elements  of his grand fantasy vision  george said where we really fell down in  terms of budget was my least favorite  scene in the entire show  in all eight seasons king robert goes  hunting martin says  four guys walking around on foot through  the woods carrying spears  and robert is giving renly a hard time  in the books  robert goes off hunting we get word he  was gored by a boar  and they bring him back and he dies so i  never did a hunting scene  but i knew what a royal hunting party  was like there would have been a hundred  guys  there would have been pavilions there  would have been huntsmen  there would have been dogs there would  have been horns blowing  that's how a king goes hunting he  wouldn't have just been walking through  the woods with three of his friends  holding spears hoping to meet a boar  but by then we could not afford horses  or dogs or the other things he mentioned  this is the scene he hated the most i'm  sorry but i find that a little hard to  believe  considering how insignificant that scene  actually is  now keep in mind i know nothing but i  may have an idea of why he said it was  this scene  instead of something from the later  seasons that greatly affected the show's  outcome for example  let's say george does hate the way jaime  lannister's story ended  or the way danny's story ended or  whoever he can't say it was his least  favorite because  then we would know his way will be  different therefore it would spoil his  books even more than they've already  been spoiled  if he said the way euron greyjoy dies or  the way cersei lannister dies was really  stupid  then we would know his version of their  final scene will be very different  i think this is why he chose a scene  from the first season that involves a  character that's already dead in his  books  that way we don't find out any other  details about how his story does end  again this is only a guess but this is  how i can justify his answer  although he may really feel that way for  all i know  he may really think that scene is worse  than all the other scenes that affected  how the story actually ends  maybe it's just me but if i were to  choose my least favorite scene  the one george rr martin chose would not  even make my top 100 worst scenes in the  series  but at the end of the day he knows way  more than i do who am i to say what  scene is the worst  let me know your thoughts down below do  you agree with george or do you think  there is another scene that's worse than  the one he chose  i would love to hear what you have to  say now before i go i do want to give a  special shout out to everyone who is  kind enough to donate to my friends  gofundme  first of all i will never be able to  thank you enough not only for your  donations but also for the condolences  for you to take a few moments out of  your day to say the things that you did  really meant a lot to me and his family  the least i can do is thank each and  every one of you who left me a message  saying you were able to help out a great  friend of mine  i want to thank billy big balls keith  struchen  josh tom neville not your little  princess  joe jay for love only jacqueline a  martin horowitz movies are terrible eric  thomas  nabil ramathullah charmaine roberts  ursachan lusty argonian maid  draz o'brien chief silverback thomas  lewis  teutonic knight matthew scott caesar  bandersnatch  calisia mde mj tiffany lewis  david cleave laura smith sandy hartcorn  ann alford rusco jamie bachmann  rewind that stephanie spain quinnida  tokun orimo eight mitch  longfinger kirsten ro